                    },
                    "message": "Updated the commit message with the use case for exposing this new information. Please take a look at the updated patchset."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you run the redfish service validator?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "Ran the redfish service validator against the specific session object.\nThe failure is on the UserType property as it is not part of the standard DMTF Session schema. \nWill revisit this once we get further guidance on the recommended approach."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This property doesn't exist in Redfish, and if it did wouldn't have these names.  Please read OEM_SCHEMAS.md, if you're trying to get these added to OEM namespaces, or the DMTF contributing docs if you're trying to add to DMTF."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "The intent is to expose the authentication backend of a user to Redfish clients. This enables clients to make informed decisions based on the user origin\nfor example, conditionally rendering operations that are only applicable to locally managed users.\n\nTo my knowledge, there is no existing standard Redfish property that conveys this information.\nCould you advise on the recommended path forward - should this fall under the OpenBMC OEM namespace?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Your next step would be to read the document I sent you above, understand it, and decide what you want to do.  I (and OpenBMC as a whole) doesn't own the Redfish specification, so if you want to add something to it, that's something you need to take up with that forum."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "Moved UserType under the OpenBMC OEM namespace. The Redfish Service Validator passes with no failures."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Read\u2026\u2026 the\u2026\u2026 documentation\u2026\u2026\n\nI will stop reviewing this code until you have."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "I've read OEM_SCHEMAS.md . I've posted on the Redfish forum to get DMTF feedback before proceeding.  Is your concern that I should wait for the forum response before pushing further changes, or is there something else I missed in the process?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
